{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l23imyud","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-15-elements-nitrogen-family","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pwhich-ordering-of-compounds-is-according-to-the-decreasin-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qazsqu3iyujckwym","content":"<p>Which ordering of compounds is according to the decreasing order of the oxidation state of nitrogen?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NO, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NO, N<sub>2</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl"},{"identifier":"C","content":"HNO<sub>3</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, NO, N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"NO, HNO<sub>3</sub>, NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, N<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>In HNO<sub>3</sub>, the oxidation state of N is +5 while in NO, it is +2. In N<sub>2</sub>, it is zero and in NH<sub>4</sub>Cl, the oxidation state of nitrogen is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>3. So, the decreasing order of oxidation state of nitrogen is</p>\n<p>HNO<sub>3</sub> &gt; NO &gt; N<sub>2</sub> &gt; NH<sub>4</sub>Cl</p>"}]}